    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0638" n="524" xml:id="pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/1550: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Istanbul</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Berry</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-31">July 31, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>275R67. On good authority I am informed that just before leaving Turkey for Italy
                    Guariglia, the new Italian Foreign Minister, told Vörnle, the Hungarian Minister
                    to Turkey, that he expected to make peace soon, if terms beneficial to Italy,
                    within the framework of the Allied unconditional surrender demand.</p>
                <p>Guariglia asked Vörnle if his government wanted him to include Hungary in the
                    peace negotiations. Vörnle cabled his conversation to Budapest and ask[ed] that
                    a [reply be?<anchor n="1" xml:id="d243-f1"/>] transmitted to Rome.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berry</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
